  "notes": [
    "The source prints increment ∆ U+2206. A visually similar Greek capital delta Δ U+0394 is not substituted.",
    "Original negative exponents and leaf indices use the source font ASCII hyphen; the former generic U+2212 fallback has been removed.",
    "Tilde in Korean prose expresses a translated range and follows the matching Korean face; it is not a source formula glyph.",
    "For S2, SymbolMT encodes its visible alpha as legacy ASCII a. Only the restored font receives a U+03B1 alias to the same original alpha glyph GID1. Original source PDF fonts remain unmodified."
